  (branch `sg-switch` = full history) and its orchestration notes. Do not
  develop there. It will move to `decoupled-consensus/archive/` when no session
  uses it.

## Builds on the Mac

- The Mac toolchain's `lean` is a throttle wrapper: `.lean` compiles share
  `LEAN_SLOTS` (default 3) machine-wide slots and are killed above
  `LEAN_CAP_GB` (default 7 GB). A long build in one project can block every
  other Lean compile. Before you assume a build is slow, check
  `ps -o etime,%cpu` on the `lean` processes.
- Run FCR builds on the NUC (`ssh nuc`). Oleans are portable: rsync
  `.lake/build` back to the Mac tree when a Mac task needs a built tree.
- Do not add a `lean_exe` target over modules that import Mathlib; linking
  compiles the whole import closure to native code. Use
  `lake env lean --run <file>.lean`.

## Proof requirements

- Committed proofs must not use `sorry`, `admit`, or project axioms. Report
  unresolved proof obligations and changes to theorem assumptions.
- Keep the project's separation of executable definitions, public statements,
  and proofs. Keep the formalization aligned with its authoritative source.
- Validate changed modules during development. Run the full project target
  before a proof milestone or a handoff. Use `lake exe cache get` when you need
  prebuilt Mathlib artifacts.
- Report the validation command, the result, and unresolved diagnostics. When
  proof soundness is part of the change, check the axioms of public theorems.
