   187	> _fgsa-conditional.md, lines 36–101:_
   188	>
   189	> Use a valid, reachable FG-SA execution, starting with the specified
   190	> initial state. An arbitrary pre-GST execution is permitted. Arbitrary
   191	> independently assigned S records, leases, or Λ records are not permitted.
   192	> There are n base seats per label and n unit-weight FG identities, as in
   193	> the two rule documents. The same static faulty set has size a. Counts
   194	> at different base labels are never added.
   195	>
   196	> ```text
   197	> h = n−a;             f = (n−1) div 3;
   198	> τ = (n+1) div 2;     q_F = (2n+2) div 3;
   199	> a ≤ f;              h ≥ q_F ≥ τ;       h > 2a;
   200	> 2q_F−n > a;         τ > a.
   201	>
   202	> Δ > 0; k ≥ 2;       L = (4k−1)Δ;
   203	> t_s = 4sΔ;          v_s = t_s+Δ;
   204	> e_s = t_s+2Δ;       z_s = t_s+3Δ;
   205	> q_s = t_s+5Δ;       d_s = t_s+6Δ;
   206	> P = 4RΔ; R ≥ 3;     T_r = rP; a_r = T_r+6Δ = d_(rR);
   207	> δ_t = 2R slots;     ρ = 2L+G+8Δ;
   208	> σ = (g+3)P+G+6Δ;   B_static = ρ+2σ.
   209	> ```
   210	>
   211	> The following premises apply through every time used in a conclusion.
   212	>
   213	> 1. All honest validators participate after GST. Each has one HEAD per
   214	>    scheduled label and one FG action per scheduled round. They process
   215	>    clocks and receipts as specified. Honest identities do not equivocate.
   216	> 2. Post-GST messages and accepted complete dependencies have strict Δ
   217	>    delivery and relay. The return-relay condition covers objects already
   218	>    accepted at GST. An emission is not a receipt, even at the sender.
   219	> 3. Blocks and signatures are authentic. Parents have smaller slots.
   220	>    Roots identify blocks uniquely. Views have the specified ancestor
   221	>    closure. Original declared support subsets remain unchanged. A later
   222	>    path receipt does not convert a raw-only declaration into support.
   223	> 4. For (L), an awake honest proposal occurs strictly after each relevant
   224	>    trigger and within G. Also use Rec(g): every inclusive round window
   225	>    `[r,r+g]` contains an honest opening whose next two **slot** proposers
   226	>    are honest. Use the rule documents' `g≥3`. The full window and every
   227	>    gate used must fit in the horizon. Strong recurrence for first finality
   228	>    is not used here. Neither K nor the debt parameter D enters (L).
   229	> 5. Honest proposals include the specified current-window rows from the
   230	>    pool and from held current-window blocks, except rows already on the
   231	>    parent chain. Use `w_F≥1`, full-row deduplication, and distinct FG
   232	>    identities. A faulty carrier may use old authentic rows. Stored
   233	>    progress bits persist until that chain advances height.
   234	> 6. The source at action r is exactly the deepest member of
   235	>    `FastWrite_i[rR] ∩ D_action` with a live deadline. An empty latest gate
   236	>    does not fall back to an earlier gate. Targets, repeats, and timeouts
   237	>    all use this source. The finality pair instead uses the actual full-view
   238	>    finality head. Its own finality pair overrides the lock at the same
   239	>    height before the height-pair branch is evaluated. Λ persists.
   240	> 7. R1 is used at every duty. Gates, saved raw results, resolution, and
   241	>    release remain unfiltered. The whole-result S guard tests all live
   242	>    leases, including excluded leases. Only a successful guarded gate
   243	>    writes S and leases. Finality does not assign to S.
   244	>
   245	> For (S), a synchronous source label means that its complete SA delivery,
   246	> return-relay, and late-test premises hold. `t_s≥GST` is a sufficient
   247	> condition. The claim is not based on `a_r≥GST` alone. The proof needs the
   248	> same receipt properties at each later label it uses. The SA definition
   249	> `SynchronousLabel` explicitly includes execution, delivery, relay, honest
   250	> majority, and horizon conditions [SA1].
   251	>
   252	> Full participation and `a≤f` are retained throughout this document to
   253	> match the recovery job. The source-to-HEAD part of (S) can use weaker
   254	> majority premises. No such weakening is needed for this interface.
