   331	> _fgsa-theorem-h.md, lines 43–112:_
   332	>
   333	> The exact recovery premises are:
   334	>
   335	> 1. The equal-size C* profile has n base seats per label and n fixed,
   336	>    unit-weight FG identities. The same static faulty set has size
   337	>    `a ≤ f = (n−1) div 3`. All h=`n−a` honest identities participate
   338	>    after GST.
   339	> 2. Objects and paths are authentic; roots are injective; parent slots
   340	>    strictly increase. Executions start from the specified initial
   341	>    state. S values, saved results, leases, and persistent DC records
   342	>    have actual event origins. Completed gates do not replay.
   343	> 3. After GST, delivery and accepted-object return relay take strictly
   344	>    less than Δ. Honest proposal delivery and proposal-view relay
   345	>    readiness hold. Receipts and clock events are processed also while
   346	>    asleep. Private faulty objects acquire a relay duty only when an
   347	>    honest reader accepts them. Every proof window fits in the horizon.
   348	> 4. Each duty computes its frame from its own R1 view. Signed proposal
   349	>    merges retain the original declared support subset. Raw tests,
   350	>    saved raw results, and release are unfiltered. The S guard tests
   351	>    all live leases, including excluded leases. Only a successful
   352	>    guarded gate changes S or writes a lease. Finality does not assign S.
   353	> 5. An awake honest proposer occurs strictly after every trigger and
   354	>    within G. For the arrival bounds, retain Rec(g): an honest opening
   355	>    and its next two slot proposers within g rounds. Honest proposals
   356	>    include current-window rows, with `w_F ≥ 1`. Use the DC causal cap,
   357	>    exact-entry quorum rules, finality lock, and persistent client rules.
   358	>
   359	> The local Theorem H needs the actual reset specified below, but does
   360	> not need a height-progress bound. Rec(g) and row inclusion are used to
   361	> obtain that reset within a deadline. No stronger recurrence for first
   362	> finality is assumed or concluded.
   363	>
   364	> ```text
   365	> τ = (n+1) div 2;      q_F = (2n+2) div 3;
   366	> h ≥ q_F ≥ τ > a;     h > 2a;             2q_F−n > a;
   367	> Δ > 0;              k ≥ 2;              L = (4k−1)Δ;
   368	> R ≥ 3;              P = 4RΔ;            g ≥ 3;
   369	> D ≥ 2;              K ≥ g+2;            δ_t = 2R slots;
   370	>
   371	> t_s = 4sΔ;          v_s = t_s+Δ;        e_s = t_s+2Δ;
   372	> z_s = t_s+3Δ;        q_s = t_s+5Δ;       d_s = t_s+6Δ;
   373	> T_r = rP;           a_r = d_(rR);
   374	> ρ = 2L+G+8Δ;        σ = (g+3)P+G+6Δ;
   375	> λ = ρ+2σ;           θ = 4Δ;             N = D+K+5.
   376	> ```
   377	>
   378	> Write `ht(B)` for the DC height of a block. Prefix order is `⪯`.
   379	> At duty d, use the blueprint's frame `(F_d,H_d,J_d,j_d,Z_d,D_d)`.
   380	> A block B is kept when `B ⪯ Z_d` or `B ∈ D_d`. The ordinary walk is
   381	> the same domain walk from Z_d, with the lease start removed. It retains
   382	> the scores, eligibility rule, and tie order.
   383	>
   384	> Let `u_0=a_(r_G+2)`, where r_G is the first action round at or after
   385	> GST. Let M be the honest archival frontier at that inclusive cut. Set
   386	> H to the first multiple of K strictly above `M+D+2`. Thus
   387	>
   388	> ```text
   389	> GST+2P ≤ u_0 < GST+3P;
   390	> M+D+3 ≤ H ≤ M+D+K+2;       H+3 ≤ M+N.
   391	> ```
   392	>
   393	> Use the actual DC consumer, with both outcomes. In the NJ outcome,
   394	> `x=H` and the retained prefix has no honest target or lock at H. In
   395	> the finalized outcome, x is its actual finalized height, `M<x≤H+1`,
   396	> and F* is the named checkpoint at x. Every block of height greater
   397	> than x extends F*. Do not replace this outcome by an assumed NJ bit.
   398	>
   399	> Let r* be the least round of an honest height-(x+1) row, let `s*=r*R`,
   400	> and let C* be its fresh fast source body. The causal cap gives a wholly
   401	> post-GST source label s*. Every honest row at height at least x+1 has
