   531	### 0.3 Glossary: F-numbers (added 2026-09-28)
   532	
   533	Two sources use the labels F1, F2, … for different facts.
   534	
   535	- The blueprint F-table (bp §3, lines 290–311) numbers DC and SA facts:
   536	  F1 honest row in each QC, F2 causal cap, F3 one justified entry per
   537	  height, F4 finality lock, F5–F10 further DC facts.
   538	- r148 (`fj-redteam.md`) numbers its own claims: F2 = a conflicting
   539	  crossing of j proves that J cannot finalize (PROVED, lines 234–258);
   540	  F3 = the converse, "retain J iff J can still finalize", is REFUTED (lines
   541	  290–309); F4 = "no timeout at H−1" as a proxy for "J can finalize" is
   542	  REFUTED and unsafe for liveness (lines 311–338); F6–F18 are its later
   543	  claims.
   544	
   545	In a pinned quote, an F-number belongs to the file of that quote. Every
   546	"F3" or "F4" in the entries of v2 means the blueprint fact: F3 is
   547	`fg.uniqueJust.v1` and F4 is `fg.finalLock.v1`. The r148 phrase
   548	"finalized-crossing law" (line 226) and "finalized crossing" are also
   549	`fg.finalLock.v1`. The FJ entry titles in §4 (F7, F9, F10, F12, F14, F17)
   550	use the r148 numbers. r148 F2 is `fj.crossingNoFinal.v1`.
   551	
   552	### 0.4 Named idealizations (added 2026-09-28)
   553	
   554	- `ViewRootInj`: distinct blocks of a view have distinct roots. This is
   555	  the collision-free root idealization, as in `fg.finalLock.v1`
   556	  (`NamedRootCollisionFree`). The lex order `(h_j, J.root)` and every tie
   557	  by root need it: DC's selector `pickUnique?` returns none on a tie of
   558	  distinct blocks (Astra plan audit G03,
   559	  `docs/audit/fg-plan-audit-report.md` lines 71–72).
