  1930	- SA discharge (registry, 2026-09-28). The SA walk is
  1931	  `get_head_in_tree` (spec lines 946–955).
  1932	  1. Start in D. The walk starts at the live root A: the deepest live
  1933	     lease target in D, else Z (spec lines 529–530, 938–944). If A is a
  1934	     lease target, A ∈ D by definition. If A = Z, then Z ∈ D: in the J
  1935	     case the J carrier (height H ≥ lo) witnesses J; in the F cases a
  1936	     frontier block at height H > h(F) extends F by `fg.finalLock.v1`
  1937	     and witnesses F at lo ≤ H (r148 lines 223–228).
  1938	  2. Stay in D. `ghost` moves only to children in its tree argument, and
  1939	     the tree is D (spec lines 907–908, 953).
  1940	  3. No stop below lo. Let X ∈ D with `σ[X].h < lo`. X has a witness
  1941	     W ∈ V with `X ⪯ W` and `σ[W].h ≥ lo`, so X ≠ W. Let Y be the child of
  1942	     X on the path to W. Then `F ⪯ X ⪯ Y`, `Z ⪯ X ⪯ Y` and `Y ⪯ W`, and V is
  1943	     ancestor-closed, so Y ∈ D. The parent X of Y has state height below
  1944	     lo, so Y is eligible without a majority (spec line 920). Thus X has an
  1945	     eligible child, and `ghost` does not return X.
  1946	  4. Stop. The tree is finite and each step goes to a child, so `ghost`
  1947	     returns a block. By steps 2 and 3 it is in D with state height ≥ lo.
  1948	  This uses the eligibility threshold lo in both viability and
  1949	  eligibility, in every phase. The start at the live root and the in-band
  1950	  choice by score stay AP data; this entry says nothing about which block
  1951	  at or above lo the walk returns.
