  2048	>
  2049	> ### 4.5 L5 — HEAD agreement after repair (PROVED)
  2050	>
  2051	> Premises: honest proposal P at `t_s` after GST and after the two-lease
  2052	> boundary of a phase, and no event in `(t_s−Δ,v_s)`.
  2053	>
  2054	> 1. **Nonempty domain.** The frontier H exceeds `ht(F)` (a finalization at
  2055	>    y has a carrier at y+1). Every height-H block extends F (crossing), and
  2056	>    extends J in an uncontested top frame. So the proposer's full domain
  2057	>    is nonempty. A viable block below lo has a viable child, which is
  2058	>    eligible, so the proposer's walk stops at A with `ht(A)≥lo`.
  2059	> 2. **Same frame.** No event in the window, and L3 for F.
  2060	> 3. **Candidates.** By L1 each child candidate at x is a proposer candidate
  2061	>    or lies on `anc(P)`. A competitor off P's path has its witness in the
  2062	>    proposer's store. Scores and eligibility are equal (same votes, same
  2063	>    lo). The path to A is viable at x through A itself, which is in `anc(P)`.
  2064	> 4. **Walk.** From x's anchor (⪯A, L4), each step picks the proposer's
  2065	>    choice: a subset of candidates that contains the maximum keeps it. At
  2066	>    A the proposer found no eligible old child, so x finds none. P is the
  2067	>    one valid current-slot child. P has no stored child. **HEAD = P.**
  2068	>
  2069	> This is SA's `honest_proposal_heads_of_ordinary_parent` with the FG frame
  2070	> added. DC's analog is `fixedHeightJustificationRoot_namedOpeningVoteStoresExtend`,
  2071	> whose SG-root premise `get_sg_root ⪯ A` becomes L4. Then r156 §5.1 gives:
  2072	> release of conflicts at `q_s`, raw result exactly P with support at least
  2073	> h at `d_s`, fast write, guard passes.
  2074	>
  2075	> ### 4.6 L6 — frame ahead of view (PROVED)
  2076	>
  2077	> When an event reaches x after `z_(s−1)` and before `v_s`, x's caches have
  2078	> it and x's block view does not. Three cases:
  2079	>
  2080	> - **Frontier rise to H without contest.** `lo=H−1`. The new carrier X
  2081	>   crossed `H−1` with a quorum that has an honest row for the entry E at
  2082	>   `H−1`. That row's source contained E and was held before its action,
  2083	>   hence before `z_(s−1)` (r156 §1.2 timing). E is in the view. So every
  2084	>   block that X witnesses keeps a view witness (E). No loss.
  2085	> - **Top J.** Root J; J has honest target rows, so J is in the view, and
  2086	>   `ht(J)=H−1=lo`. The domain is J's subtree. No empty domain.
  2087	> - **Contest, or a rise into a contest.** `lo=H`. The view can lack every
  2088	>   height-H block. Then the view domain is empty and the HEAD returns the
  2089	>   anchor. DC does the same: an empty filtered view returns the SG root.
  2090	>
  2091	> In each case the slot is the one charged by L2. The anchor case cannot
  2092	> break L8: in a P1 run the anchor is a live lease that extends the armed
  2093	> block B (§4.8).
