  2097	> ### 9.4 The root (anchor) fallback on the SA side (C5, PROVED)
  2098	>
  2099	> **When it occurs.** A HEAD falls back to its anchor X (the FG root if no
  2100	> live lease is in the full domain) only when its frozen domain is empty.
  2101	> If the HEAD's live frame equals the proposer's, P's path carries A with
  2102	> `ht(A)≥lo`, so the domain is not empty (L5 step 3). F moves never empty it
  2103	> (C1). A top J is in the view at height lo, and in a band rise the crossed
  2104	> entry E is in the view (L6). So a fallback needs an event in `(t_s−Δ,v_s)`
  2105	> that puts the node in a contest frame (first contest witness, or a rise
  2106	> into a contest). By L2 this is at most two slots per frontier, and before
  2107	> the reset only frontiers M and M+1 count: at most four slots in all.
  2108	> After the reset no contest exists above M+1, so no fallback occurs.
