  3956	## 4. `SimplexFG.fj` — FJ root rule, own frame and interface (audit W06)
  3957	
  3958	FJ changes the frame rule: a frontier test, root F and band `{H}` in a
  3959	contest. It is a module variant, not a base selector. HNI is NOT the FJ
  3960	interface. FJ can keep a height-(M+1) source that does not extend an old
  3961	justified entry at M; this is a failure of HNI(M+1).(h1), while FJ's filter
  3962	still protects the source:
  3963	
  3964	> _fgsa-no-nj-opus.md, lines 612–620:_
  3965	>
  3966	> **N14: NJ-free reset — PROVED.** Under FJ every step of a descent chain
  3967	> has `x ≥ σ[C].h`. So every abandoned post-GST source has height at most
  3968	> M (§3.3). Every honest row at height ≥ M+1 has a synchronous label, so
  3969	> its source is extended by every honest HEAD from its label on. The next
  3970	> unanimous batch then puts it in every S by `t_s+10Δ` (fgsa-fast-opus
  3971	> §5.1 step 7). This is Lemma R with `x=M` and no NJ. It also follows the
  3972	> proof in fgsa-adjudicate §4: the only change is its "old J at x" clause.
  3973	> Under FJ an old J at M cannot pass a source C* at M+1, because C* is a
  3974	> frontier block that does not extend it.
  3975	
  3976	Thus `fg.HNI.v1`, `fg.H19.v1`, `fg.HNIb.v1`, `fg.trunk.v1`,
  3977	`fg.oneBullet.v1` (now `fg.oneBullet.core.v1`), `fg.base.finalized.v1`,
  3978	`fg.base.nj.v1` and `fg.baseSel.nj.v1` do not apply to FJ. The FJ
  3979	noninterference interface is `fj.descent.v1`, `fj.canonical.v1` (F9),
  3980	`fj.inBandLock.v1` (F10) and `fj.twoChanges.v1` (F12; now
  3981	`fj.twoChanges.core.v1` with `comp.settle.v1`); its reset witness is
  3982	`fj.reset.v1`. The `both` entries `fg.provenance.v2`,
  3983	`fg.causalCap.core.v1`, `fg.uniqueJust.v1`, `fg.finalLock.v1`,
  3984	`fg.frameCompat.v1`, `comp.provenance.v1`, `comp.settle.v1` and
  3985	`comp.cut.v1` apply to FJ. The FJ cap M
  3986	is the cap on old honest rows (`env.r148`); it is at most DC's archival
  3987	M0. r151 calls this cap μ and calls M0 simply M.
