  2091	  A reference is structured data: `.ap` and `.external` carry the registry id in their own field, and the note is a second field, so no id is read from prose (Astra Q01). AP data and comp run facts with no registry id are `.apData` and `.runFact`. Use the real namespaces of the Lean names (`AvailableChain.KitFG.…`). Set each clause to what Tasks 5–13 reported: if a statement changed, or a proof needed an extra hypothesis, change its clause and report it. Add one `example` per Lean name that elaborates it, for example `example := @AvailableChain.KitFG.accountable`. The build then fails when a name moves. Do not pin a name to an `ap.*` id.
  2092	- [ ] **Step 2: Write `scripts/FGPinIds.lean` and `scripts/check-fg-pins.sh`.** No step parses Lean text (Astra P01, Q01–Q03). ONE Lean script prints the manifest of the ELABORATED pin table (`emitManifest`, Step 1): the sources with their hashes, the pin ids, the active `.ap` and `.external` ids, the `notFormalized` ids, and an `END` trailer with the counts. The shell check reads only that output.
