-  `idTokens` uses only `List Char` operations: in Lean v4.30 `String.split` and `String.dropRightWhile` return iterators and slices. Use the real namespaces of the Lean names (`AvailableChain.KitFG.…`). Set each clause to what Tasks 5–13 reported: if a statement changed, or a proof needed an extra hypothesis, change its clause and report it. Add one `example` per Lean name that elaborates it, for example `example := @AvailableChain.KitFG.accountable`. The build then fails when a name moves. Do not pin a name to an `ap.*` id.
-- [ ] **Step 2: Write `scripts/FGPinIds.lean` and `scripts/check-fg-pins.sh`.** The pin check reads the ids from the ELABORATED `Pins.lean` (Astra P01): a textual `grep` of `id := "…"` misses valid Lean such as `id:="fj.frame.v2"`, and it does not see the ids in `.ap` and `.external` clauses.
+  A reference is structured data: `.ap` and `.external` carry the registry id in their own field, and the note is a second field, so no id is read from prose (Astra Q01). AP data and comp run facts with no registry id are `.apData` and `.runFact`. Use the real namespaces of the Lean names (`AvailableChain.KitFG.…`). Set each clause to what Tasks 5–13 reported: if a statement changed, or a proof needed an extra hypothesis, change its clause and report it. Add one `example` per Lean name that elaborates it, for example `example := @AvailableChain.KitFG.accountable`. The build then fails when a name moves. Do not pin a name to an `ap.*` id.
